<title>UK: HORSE RACING-KING GEORGE VI &amp; QUEEN ELIZABETH RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-KING GEORGE VI &amp; QUEEN ELIZABETH RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>ASCOT, England 1997-07-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the King George VI and Queen Elizabeth Diamond Stakes, a group one race for three-year-olds and upwards, run over one and a half miles (2.4 km) on Saturday:</p>
<p> 1. Swain     16-1 (ridden by John Reid)</p>
<p>2. Pilsudski  6-1 (Michael Kinane)</p>
<p>3. Helissio  11-10 favourite (Cash Asmussen)</p>
<p>Eight ran.</p>
<p>Distances: One length, one and a quarter lengths.</p>
<p>Winner owned by Godolphin, trained by Saeed Bin Suroor at Newmarket in England.</p>
<p>Value to winner: 294,600 pounds sterling ($489,000)</p>
